{
  // Idle skeletons crumbling back into their piles, and the Skeleton King's slam shrapnel: run from OpenGLTest/ with
  //   VOXEL_TIME=147 VOXEL_SCRIPT=visual-examples/tower-idle-shrapnel.json
  // Shots land in visual/tower-idle-shrapnel/. The tower is battle-tower.json's (center (2920, -1411), floor 0's slab at
  // y 10, roof at y 45, altar cell (2920, 46, -1411)). Beside floor 0's pile at (2916, -1411) (the only pile within
  // MobConfig.SkeletonPileTriggerBlocks of this spot) the player turns survival twice, a wave's cooldown apart, so the
  // pile raises both its waves and is spent (the sweep clears its block); between and after those blinks the player is
  // creative (immune, so the pile stays asleep and the skeletons only face it). The damage step wounds both skeletons
  // and the shot looks up at their hearts. Then the player flies well past the notice radius (but inside the despawn
  // radius and the tower leash) for longer than MobConfig.SkeletonPileReturnIdleSeconds, so both crumble back into the
  // floor (owed). Back on floor 0 flying the floor is empty. Turning creative off (which also ends flight; a plain
  // "fly off" keeps creative, so the player would stay immune and no pile would wake) lands a survival player: a spent
  // pile raises only owed skeletons, so the one that rises at its spot is a crumbled one raised again, at full health.
  // Then, like skeleton-king.json, the floors are cleared, the altar raises the king, and its slam is filmed from the
  // shoulder view (wind-up, the first shards out) and then from above, where the shards fly out all round (the
  // player has moved away, so none is stopped on it).
  // Shots: hurt, crumbled, risen_again, slam_windup, slam_shards, slam_spread, slam_spread_late.
  "steps": [
    { "op": "fly", "on": true },
